{"in":{"type":"control_response","response":{"subtype":"success","request_id":"3eefb6c6-99f8-407c-99e5-e566551fed75","response":{"mcp_response":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"permission_prompt","description":"Internal to Avala: answers the permission prompts of Claude Code with Avala\u0027s policy. Never call it yourself.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool_name":{"type":"string"},"input":{"type":"object"},"tool_use_id":{"type":"string"}}}},{"name":"propose_follow_up","description":"Propose a follow-up task for the harness to run after this job, as a new job with its own review. The harness accepts or refuses it by its policy and tells you which.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"instruction":{"type":"string","description":"The instruction of the follow-up job, complete enough to be done on its own."},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"Why the follow-up is needed."}},"required":["instruction"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"canvas","description":"Draw a canvas the user sees beside the conversation: a diagram, a chart, a screen, a design or a document. Give it a title, one of the offered media types and its full content. Each call draws a new canvas.\nOffered media types:\n- image/svg\u002Bxml (SVG): Draw every diagram, chart, flow, screen or design as SVG.\n- text/markdown (Markdown): Write notes, tables, plans and reports as Markdown.\n- text/vnd.mermaid (Mermaid): Write a standard flowchart, sequence, state, class or entity-relationship diagram as Mermaid when its syntax fits; Avala draws it in the app\u0027s theme.\nA canvas in any other media type is not drawn: the user only sees its source.\nSVG animations written in SMIL, such as \u003Canimate\u003E, \u003CanimateTransform\u003E, \u003CanimateMotion\u003E and \u003Cset\u003E, play on the canvas, so a chart may grow or a flow may move; CSS keyframes and scripts do not run, and nothing on a canvas responds to input. Something that must respond to input, such as an interactive chart, a three.js scene or an app, is a page instead: when Avala offers its preview, serve the page and give the person its URL, which Avala shows in its preview pane; otherwise write a self-contained HTML file in the working directory and give the person its path, which Avala offers to open.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","description":"A short title shown above the canvas."},"mediaType":{"type":"string","enum":["image/svg\u002Bxml","text/markdown","text/vnd.mermaid"],"description":"How the content is drawn: one of the media types Avala offers."},"content":{"type":"string","description":"The full content of the canvas."}},"required":["title","mediaType","content"],"additionalProperties":false},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"subagents","description":"List every sub-agent of your job with its real state, as Avala knows it: the ones your harness ran inside your session, including those of earlier sessions of this job lost when it ended, and the ones you delegated to another harness with delegate. Each has its name, its kind, inProcess or crossHarness, its state, working, waiting, completed, failed, stopped or lost, and its status, which says what a waiting one waits for; a crossHarness one also names its job, connection and harness.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}}]}}}}}}
